RISC3D test kit 23 (prototype, 14 November 2026)
================================================

TORCS through RISC3D still draws its car plain yellow and the scenery
smeared. Kit 22's log showed every texture TORCS loads arriving
complete (208 of them, every mipmap level, no GL errors), and riscos-
mesa's texture tests all pass on the GPU. So the next step is to record
exactly what TORCS sends, and draw it again: on the Pi's GPU, in Linux's
software renderer on the Pi, and on the build machine. Whichever of
those draws the yellow car shows where the fault is.

This kit's rol-3d (0.12, in riscos-risc3d 0.12-1) can record.

Steps
-----
 1. Copy RISC3DTest to HardDisc4 (unzip it there, replacing kit 22).
 2. In RiSH's Root shell:
      apt-get install /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/riscos-risc3d_0.12-1_arm64.deb
      sh /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/check off
      sh /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/record on 250
 3. Run TORCS through RISC3D: start a race straight away and drive for
    about 20 seconds (until the car has been on screen a while), then
    quit TORCS.
 4. In RiSH's Root shell:
      sh /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/record off
    It lists the recordings: the big one is TORCS's.
 5. Draw it again, here:
      sh /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/replay /riscos/3d/recorded/ctx-NNN.r3d /25
    (NNN from the list.) It writes ReplayGPU-25, -50, ... and
    ReplaySoft-25, -50, ... into RISC3DTest: PPM pictures.

Please send
-----------
The recording (/riscos/3d/recorded/ctx-NNN.r3d: copy it to the Mac; it
may be a few hundred MB), and a ReplayGPU and a ReplaySoft picture of a
frame where the car shows.
